! mcp_bootstrap_p216.strap -- MCP printed page 216: the V (input program)
! card-reader service, V REE4 .. V RDIO, ending in a B,DMCP / ,DRD call.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.223, read at 400 dpi (900 dpi for the
! doubtful glyphs).  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000132  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 216"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 224201, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  Contiguous from 224201.00 to 224237.00 (a half word), 51
! lines, every line number printed with a "*".  The vision reading of
! p.215 ends 224200.40 (a half word: SV,V T2,V X1(V U)), so line 1's .00
! continues it; p.217's line 1 reads 224237.40 (",V CRD"), continuing
! line 51.
!   line  7      CNOP, at 224204.00 -- no location printed, emits nothing.
!   line  8      V REE6 (IQS*)DD(BU,8,8), 24 characters, 3 words.
!   lines 25-26  VF,V REE6 (224204.00+) and CF,3 (000003).
!   lines 23-24, 50-51  B,DMCP followed by a null-operation parameter card.
!
! THE REMARK COLUMN prints "-0168" .. "-0211", one per source card, and
! the card serials run 0A000132 .. 0A000177 (the first glyph is the
! drum's worn D or 0; the header prints "CA000132").  Five serials are
! printed on TWO lines each -- 149 (lines 18,19), 153 (23,24), 174
! (45,46), 176 (48,49), 177 (50,51) -- and in every pair the first line
! prints no remark and the second prints its remark shifted left, the
! way a second statement on one card would.  Line 34 (serial 163) prints
! no remark.  Recorded, not explained.  Lines 15 and 35 print a "*" after
! the LOCATION (as p.197 line 11).
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY SOMETHING OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!  * Line 4 prints "B,V IO(V U)" with a nearly closed round glyph.  The
!    only such symbol is p.213 line 17 "V IC SYN,V NX.V H" = 000005.40
!    (read off PDF p.220 for this deck), and the binary 000005.50 is
!    exactly V IC + B's .10.  Written VID, p.213's spelling of its label
!    (that page reads a worn D; the glyph is not settled on either page).
!  * "V ECFX" (line 22) / "V EOFX" (lines 35, 43): all three compile
!    224372.32, the same symbol.  Labels "V ECFB" (28) and "V ECFN" (36)
!    print open; p.215's references (lines 6, 14, vision) read V EOFN and
!    V EOFB.  EOF (end of file) is the English; written VEOFX/VEOFB/VEOFN.
!  * "V NCP" (lines 30, 35, 36, 41) / "V NOP" (28, 33, 38): one symbol,
!    224157.40 (p.215 line 18).  Written VNOP.
!  * Line 46 "B,V CCM" is V COM (p.228 line 15, 224702.00 = .10 less);
!    line 49 "B,V MC" is V MD (D's stem worn; p.228 line 26, 224707.40).
!  * Line 44's label prints "V RDQ" with a clear Q tail at 900 dpi; kept
!    as RDQ.  NOTE p.224 line 45 (vision) reads "B,V RDO" at 224233.50 =
!    this label + .10 -- the coordinator should settle Q vs O there.
!  * Hex bytes printed "CC"/"0C" on lines 6, 10, 11 (h2), 28 (h2), 35 (h2)
!    are 00 -- the open round 0 this page prints in its octal fields too
!    (000000 prints "CCCCCC" on lines 1, 5, 18, 45, 48).  See the CHECKs.
!  * The h2 bytes of the six bit-branch rows (11, 28, 35, 36, 43 and 22's
!    "02") are indistinguishable "0C"/"CC" glyph pairs at 900 dpi.  The
!    statement settles them: BZB (lines 11, 28, 36) assembles 00, and
!    BZB1 (lines 35, 43, the "1" printed plainly) assembles 0C -- the
!    one-variant's bit in the low nibble.

! --- external symbols -----------------------------------------------------
! The V index/field SYNs are p.213's (read off its image, PDF p.220).
VU      SYN, $3                      ! p.213 line 25 "V U SYN,$3"  (000023.00)
VP      SYN, $1                      ! p.213 line 26 "V P SYN,$1"
VT1     SYN, $4                      ! p.213 line 27
VT5     SYN, $9                      ! p.213 line 28
VT2     SYN, $6                      ! p.213 line 29
VT3     SYN, $7                      ! p.213 line 30
VX      SYN, (8)0.0                  ! p.213 line 11 "V X SYN,0"
VX1     SYN, (8)0.40                 ! p.213 line 12 "SYN,V X.V H" prints 000000.40
VX2R    SYN, (8)2.0                  ! p.213 line 14 prints 000002.00
VNX     SYN, (8)5.0                  ! p.213 line 16 prints 000005.00
VID     SYN, (8)5.40                 ! p.213 line 17 "V ID" (read VID there; ink IC/IO/ID unsettled) prints 000005.40
VF      SYN, (8)0.40                 ! p.213 line 6 "V F SYN,.32"
DMCP    SYN, 32.0                    ! landed p.108
DCOMM   SYN, 35.32                   ! landed p.105
DRD     SYN, 1.0                     ! landed p.104
